; spring_trial.room - the spring song trials (docs/maps/README.md), left to right.
; Tested by tests/scenes/world/rooms/trials/spring_trial_test.gd. Base movement,
; a single jump.
;
; 1. The dry basin (design 02 section 8, Primavera Logico 2): climb the steps,
;    drop in. The passage (three cells tall) high in the far wall is out of reach
;    from the floor, from the step and from the wall's top (the basin is too
;    wide to jump). Chuva fills the basin; the log, lying by the far wall,
;    rides the water up to the passage and Ivo steps off it into it. The step inside means a dry basin never traps anyone.
; 2. The dry moat (Combinado 1, Chuva then Congelar): too wide to jump, shallow
;    enough to climb out of. Chuva fills it; Congelar played at its edge while
;    the water is high makes it a floor - ice where there was no water. The
;    water drains under the ice while the thaw comes from the origin: two
;    clocks. A fall lands on the dry floor, which can be climbed out of.
; 3. The earth shaft (Primavera Espacial 2): an opening high in the far wall,
;    out of reach from the floor; the near wall runs to the ceiling. Enraizar
;    from the floor between the walls grows a web of roots across the shaft;
;    Ivo climbs it (up held to grab) and steps into the opening.
; 4. The root bridge (Primavera Espacial 1): a chasm too wide to jump over
;    water. From the near bank Enraizar's pulse cannot reach the far one; from
;    the low stone ledge (col 49) it covers both banks, and Ivo jumps up through
;    the bridge and crosses before it breaks at the tips. The far bank is out
;    of reach from the ledge; the near bank is not, so it never traps.
; 5. The wet bridge (design 02 section 7.4, Chuva then Enraizar): a 12-cell
;    chasm, wider than a dry root bridge (10 cells) and within a wet one (14).
;    From the stone ledge (col 65) Enraizar covers both banks but grows
;    nothing; played inside a Chuva pulse, the wet earth lets the bridge
;    cross, and once joined it holds while Enraizar does. The ledge is too
;    deep to jump to the far bank; the stone step (col 61) leads back to the
;    near bank, or up through the bridge. From the far bank the way back is a
;    running jump onto the ledge.

[room]
origin = 0, -16

